# District Heating Forecaster — Project Context

## What this app is
Streamlit dashboard (`app.py`) for Flensburg district heating demand forecasting.
- **Model**: 48 direct LightGBM models, one per horizon h=1…48h
- **Confidence bands**: Monte Carlo with NWP σ(h) noise, 80% CI
- **Weather**: Open-Meteo API (live NWP) or fallback to observed CSV data
- **Dataset**: Zenodo 17177421 · 2020–2024 · train 2020–2023 · test 2024
- **Repo**: https://github.com/herbvibe/district-heating-forecaster

## Architecture (`src/`)
- `data.py` — raw CSV loading, feature engineering (`MH_FEATURES`, 25–30 cols)
- `model.py` — `simulate_forecast()`, `compute_mape()`, `BEST_PARAMS`
- `model_registry.py` — JSON-backed model version registry
- `weather.py` — Open-Meteo wrapper (forecast + historical endpoints)
- `train_multi_horizon.py` — CLI to retrain all 48 models

## Hard constraints
- `MH_FEATURES` is fixed — adding/removing features requires retraining all 48 models
- `init()` uses `@st.cache_resource` — **server must be fully restarted** after retraining
- Never work directly on `main`; branch first (`feature/` or `experiment/` prefix)
- Production inference path is always `get_mh_forecast_window()` — never extend the legacy single-model fallback

## Brand / UI conventions
**Palette constants** (defined near top of `app.py`):
- `NAVY #11224D` — primary text, history lines
- `PINK #E31B54` — accent, temperature axis
- `TEAL #2EC4B6` — wind speed, `ACCENT2`
- `PURPLE #7B2CBF` — humidity, override zones
- `FORECAST #263884` — demand forecast median + CI band
- `NOW_COL GRAY_MID` — "now" vertical line (grey)
- `FORECAST_SHADE rgba(17,34,77,0.07)` — light grey fill right of "now"
- `BAND_COL rgba(38,56,132,0.18)` — 80% CI fill

**Font**: Inter (Google Fonts), loaded via `_inject_brand_styles()`

**Logo**: `assets/gradyent-logo.svg` (official SVG from gradyent.ai, navy wordmark)

## Layout
- **Header**: logo (left) + "Heating Demand Forecast - Flensburg" (right of logo)
- **Sidebar top**: Avg MAPE + Avg MAE metrics → model version selector → snapshot date/hour → weather toggle → retrain expander
- **Sidebar bottom**: plain caption rows (snapshot, horizon, model, training info)
- **Main area**: header row → KPI metrics → Plotly chart (3 subplots: demand / temp+wind / cloud+humidity) → horizon toggle → manual override expander
- **Chart legends**: transparent background (no white boxes)
